sentences.l:
And now he would have dragged him off and won boundless glory,
if not then sharply had noticed the daughter of Zeus, Aphrodite,
who for him broke the strap of an ox slain with force;

Is it somewhere farther, of well-inhabited cities,
that you will lead me, either of Phrygia or of lovely Maeonia,
if some man dear to you is there too among speech-dividing men;

sentences.t:
οὕνεκα δὴ νῦν δῖον Ἀλέξανδρον Μενέλαος
νικήσας ἐθέλει στυγερὴν ἐμὲ οἴκαδ’ ἄγεσθαι,
τοὔνεκα δὴ νῦν δεῦρο δολοφρονέουσα παρέστης;

sentences.tr:
houneka dē nyn dion Alexandron Menelaos
nikēsas ethelei stygerēn eme oikad’ agesthai,
touneka dē nyn deuro dolophroneousa parestēs;

sentences.l:
So she spoke, and was afraid Helen, sprung of Zeus,
and went, covering herself with the bright, shining robe,
in silence, and all the Trojan women she escaped the notice of;
